# Async and Concurrency Challenges with Correlation IDs

## The Core Problem

When correlation IDs are stored in **ThreadLocal** variables, they work fine for synchronous request processing. However, in asynchronous systems, multi-threaded environments, and thread pools, correlation IDs can get lost or mixed up between requests.

## Why ThreadLocal Fails

### Synchronous Request Processing (Works Fine)

```
Request 1 comes in on Thread A
├─ ThreadLocal.set(correlation_id_1)
├─ Process request
├─ All logs include correlation_id_1
└─ ThreadLocal.clear()

Request 2 comes in on Thread B
├─ ThreadLocal.set(correlation_id_2)
├─ Process request
├─ All logs include correlation_id_2
└─ ThreadLocal.clear()
```

✅ **No issues**: Each request gets its own thread with isolated ThreadLocal

### Thread Pool Scenario (Breaks)

```
Thread Pool Created: 10 worker threads

Request 1 arrives:
├─ Assigned to Worker Thread A
├─ ThreadLocal.set(correlation_id_1)
├─ Process request
├─ ThreadLocal.clear()
└─ Worker Thread A returns to pool

Request 2 arrives (immediately):
├─ Assigned to Worker Thread A again (reused from pool)
├─ ThreadLocal NOT inherited (worker already exists)
├─ New ThreadLocal.set(correlation_id_2)
├─ But what if ThreadLocal wasn't fully cleared?
└─ Logs might show old correlation_id_1 mixed with correlation_id_2
```

❌ **Problem**: ThreadLocal values from previous requests can bleed through

### Async/Await (Breaks Worse)

```javascript
// Node.js example
async function processRequest(req, res) {
  const correlationId = req.headers['x-correlation-id'];
  asyncLocalStorage.run({ correlationId }, async () => {
    logger.info('Starting request'); // ✅ correlation_id present

    // Async operation that doesn't preserve context
    await someAsyncOperation(); // 🔴 Context lost here!

    logger.info('Finishing request'); // ❌ correlation_id MISSING
  });
}
```

❌ **Problem**: Async operations lose the execution context

## Common Failure Patterns

### Pattern 1: Forgotten Context Cleanup

```java
// WRONG - context not cleared
@Component
public class BadFilter extends OncePerRequestFilter {
    @Override
    protected void doFilterInternal(HttpServletRequest request,
                                   HttpServletResponse response,
                                   FilterChain filterChain) throws ServletException, IOException {
        String correlationId = request.getHeader("X-Correlation-ID");
        MDC.put("correlation_id", correlationId);
        filterChain.doFilter(request, response);
        // ❌ Forgot to clear! Next request may see this correlation_id
    }
}

// CORRECT - always cleanup
@Component
public class GoodFilter extends OncePerRequestFilter {
    @Override
    protected void doFilterInternal(HttpServletRequest request,
                                   HttpServletResponse response,
                                   FilterChain filterChain) throws ServletException, IOException {
        String correlationId = request.getHeader("X-Correlation-ID");
        MDC.put("correlation_id", correlationId);
        try {
            filterChain.doFilter(request, response);
        } finally {
            MDC.remove("correlation_id"); // ✅ Always cleanup
        }
    }
}
```

### Pattern 2: Async Methods Without Decorator

```java
// WRONG - correlation_id lost in async thread
@Service
public class BadAsyncService {
    @Async
    public void processOrderAsync(String orderId) {
        // ❌ MDC from original request thread is NOT inherited
        logger.info("Processing order"); // Missing correlation_id!
    }
}

// CORRECT - configure TaskDecorator
@Configuration
public class AsyncConfiguration implements AsyncConfigurer {
    @Override
    public Executor getAsyncExecutor() {
        ThreadPoolTaskExecutor executor = new ThreadPoolTaskExecutor();
        executor.setTaskDecorator(new ContextPropagatingDecorator());
        executor.initialize();
        return executor;
    }

    public static class ContextPropagatingDecorator implements TaskDecorator {
        @Override
        public Runnable decorate(Runnable runnable) {
            Map<String, String> contextMap = MDC.getCopyOfContextMap();
            return () -> {
                if (contextMap != null) {
                    MDC.setContextMap(contextMap);
                } else {
                    MDC.clear();
                }
                try {
                    runnable.run();
                } finally {
                    MDC.clear();
                }
            };
        }
    }

    @Service
    public class GoodAsyncService {
        @Async
        public void processOrderAsync(String orderId) {
            // ✅ Correlation_id properly propagated
            logger.info("Processing order");
        }
    }
}
```

### Pattern 3: Message Queue Operations

```java
// WRONG - no correlation context
@KafkaListener(topics = "orders")
public void processOrder(String message) {
    // ❌ Correlation ID from original request is lost
    // Message arrived on different thread with no context
    logger.info("Processing order from queue"); // No correlation_id
}

// CORRECT - extract and propagate from message
@KafkaListener(topics = "orders")
public void processOrder(String message, @Header("X-Correlation-ID") String correlationId) {
    MDC.put("correlation_id", correlationId);
    try {
        logger.info("Processing order from queue"); // ✅ Has correlation_id
    } finally {
        MDC.clear();
    }
}
```

### Pattern 4: Retry Logic

```java
// WRONG - context lost on retry
public String callDownstreamService() {
    try {
        return restTemplate.getForObject(url, String.class);
    } catch (Exception e) {
        // ❌ Retry happens on different thread, loses MDC
        return retry();
    }
}

// CORRECT - use resilience4j with context propagation
@Service
public class ResilientService {
    private final Resilience4jCircuitBreakerFactory factory;

    public String callDownstreamService() {
        Retry retry = factory.create("order-service-retry",
            RetryConfig.custom()
                .retryExceptions(IOException.class)
                .build());

        // ✅ resilience4j can be configured to preserve MDC
        return Decorators.retry(retry)
            .decorate(() -> restTemplate.getForObject(url, String.class))
            .execute();
    }
}
```

## Technology-Specific Solutions

### Java/Spring Boot: TransmittableThreadLocal (TTL)

**Problem**: InheritableThreadLocal doesn't work with thread pools

**Solution**: Use `TransmittableThreadLocal` library

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>com.alibaba</groupId>
    <artifactId>transmittable-thread-local</artifactId>
    <version>2.14.2</version>
</dependency>
```

```java
// Setup TTL for MDC
TransmittableThreadLocal<Map<String, String>> mdcTtl = new TransmittableThreadLocal<>();

// Configure thread pool to use TTL
@Bean
public Executor taskExecutor() {
    ThreadPoolTaskExecutor executor = new ThreadPoolTaskExecutor();
    executor.setTaskDecorator(new TtlTaskDecorator());
    executor.initialize();
    return executor;
}

public class TtlTaskDecorator implements TaskDecorator {
    @Override
    public Runnable decorate(Runnable runnable) {
        // TTL automatically handles context propagation
        return TtlRunnable.get(runnable);
    }
}
```

### Python: contextvars (Built-in)

**Solution**: Python 3.7+ includes `contextvars` for async-safe context

```python
import contextvars
import asyncio

# Define context variable
correlation_id_var = contextvars.ContextVar('correlation_id')

# In middleware
async def bind_correlation_id(request, call_next):
    correlation_id = request.headers.get('X-Correlation-ID')
    token = correlation_id_var.set(correlation_id) # ✅ Set for this context
    try:
        response = await call_next(request)
    finally:
        correlation_id_var.reset(token) # ✅ Clean up

# In any async function
async def process_order(order_id: str):
    corr_id = correlation_id_var.get() # ✅ Works in any async context
    logger.info("Processing", correlation_id=corr_id)

    # Even nested async calls work
    await asyncio.gather(
        validate_order(order_id),
        check_inventory(order_id)
    ) # ✅ Both preserve correlation_id
```

### Node.js: AsyncLocalStorage or AsyncContext

**Solution**: Use `AsyncLocalStorage` for async context

```javascript
const { AsyncLocalStorage } = require('async_hooks');

const correlationIdStore = new AsyncLocalStorage();

// Middleware
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const correlationId = req.headers['x-correlation-id'];
  correlationIdStore.run({ correlationId }, () => {
    next();
  });
});

// Get logger with correlation_id
function getLogger() {
  const context = correlationIdStore.getStore();
  return logger.child({ correlation_id: context?.correlationId });
}

// Usage - works with promises and async/await
app.get('/orders/:id', async (req, res) => {
  getLogger().info('Fetching order'); // ✅ correlation_id present

  const inventory = await fetch('http://inventory-service/check');

  getLogger().info('Inventory checked'); // ✅ Still present
  res.json({});
});

// Background tasks - must explicitly propagate
async function processOrderAsync(correlationId) {
  await correlationIdStore.run({ correlationId }, async () => {
    getLogger().info('Processing background order'); // ✅ Has correlation_id
    await someAsyncWork();
  });
}
```

## Testing Correlation ID Propagation

### Unit Test: Verify Context Cleanup

```java
@Test
void testMDCIsCleanedAfterRequest() {
    // Before
    assertNull(MDC.get("correlation_id"));

    // Simulate request with correlation_id
    String testId = "test-123";
    MDC.put("correlation_id", testId);
    assertEquals(testId, MDC.get("correlation_id"));

    // After cleanup (as filter should do)
    MDC.clear();

    // Verify cleaned
    assertNull(MDC.get("correlation_id"));
}
```

### Integration Test: Async Propagation

```java
@Test
void testCorrelationIdPropagatedToAsyncTask() throws Exception {
    String correlationId = "async-test-123";
    MDC.put("correlation_id", correlationId);

    AtomicReference<String> asyncMdcValue = new AtomicReference<>();

    asyncService.processAsync(() -> {
        asyncMdcValue.set(MDC.get("correlation_id"));
    });

    // Wait for async completion
    Thread.sleep(100);

    assertEquals(correlationId, asyncMdcValue.get());
    MDC.clear();
}
```

### End-to-End Test: Service Boundary

```javascript
describe('Correlation ID Propagation', () => {
  it('should propagate correlation_id across service calls', async () => {
    const correlationId = 'e2e-test-123';

    const response1 = await request(app)
      .get('/orders')
      .set('X-Correlation-ID', correlationId);

    // Extract correlation_id from log output
    const logs = captureConsoleOutput();
    expect(logs).toContain(correlationId);

    // Call downstream service
    const response2 = await request(downstreamService)
      .get('/inventory')
      .set('X-Correlation-ID', correlationId);

    const downstreamLogs = captureConsoleOutput(downstreamService);
    expect(downstreamLogs).toContain(correlationId);
  });

  it('should generate new correlation_id if header missing', async () => {
    const response = await request(app).get('/orders');

    const logs = captureConsoleOutput();
    // Should have some correlation_id (UUID format)
    expect(logs).toMatch(/correlation_id":"[a-f0-9\-]{36}/);
  });
});
```

## Checklist for Async Safety

- [ ] All ThreadLocal usage has try-finally cleanup
- [ ] TaskDecorator configured for thread pools (@Async, custom executors)
- [ ] contextvars/AsyncLocalStorage used for async code (not ThreadLocal)
- [ ] Message queue handlers extract correlation_id from headers
- [ ] Retry logic preserves MDC/context
- [ ] Background jobs receive correlation_id explicitly
- [ ] Integration tests verify async propagation
- [ ] No correlation_id bleeding between unrelated requests
- [ ] Context cleared after each request

