     1→# Async and Concurrency Challenges with Correlation IDs
     2→
     3→## The Core Problem
     4→
     5→When correlation IDs are stored in **ThreadLocal** variables, they work fine for synchronous request processing. However, in asynchronous systems, multi-threaded environments, and thread pools, correlation IDs can get lost or mixed up between requests.
     6→
     7→## Why ThreadLocal Fails
     8→
     9→### Synchronous Request Processing (Works Fine)
    10→
    11→```
    12→Request 1 comes in on Thread A
    13→├─ ThreadLocal.set(correlation_id_1)
    14→├─ Process request
    15→├─ All logs include correlation_id_1
    16→└─ ThreadLocal.clear()
    17→
    18→Request 2 comes in on Thread B
    19→├─ ThreadLocal.set(correlation_id_2)
    20→├─ Process request
    21→├─ All logs include correlation_id_2
    22→└─ ThreadLocal.clear()
    23→```
    24→
    25→✅ **No issues**: Each request gets its own thread with isolated ThreadLocal
    26→
    27→### Thread Pool Scenario (Breaks)
    28→
    29→```
    30→Thread Pool Created: 10 worker threads
    31→
    32→Request 1 arrives:
    33→├─ Assigned to Worker Thread A
    34→├─ ThreadLocal.set(correlation_id_1)
    35→├─ Process request
    36→├─ ThreadLocal.clear()
    37→└─ Worker Thread A returns to pool
    38→
    39→Request 2 arrives (immediately):
    40→├─ Assigned to Worker Thread A again (reused from pool)
    41→├─ ThreadLocal NOT inherited (worker already exists)
    42→├─ New ThreadLocal.set(correlation_id_2)
    43→├─ But what if ThreadLocal wasn't fully cleared?
    44→└─ Logs might show old correlation_id_1 mixed with correlation_id_2
    45→```
    46→
    47→❌ **Problem**: ThreadLocal values from previous requests can bleed through
    48→
    49→### Async/Await (Breaks Worse)
    50→
    51→```javascript
    52→// Node.js example
    53→async function processRequest(req, res) {
    54→  const correlationId = req.headers['x-correlation-id'];
    55→  asyncLocalStorage.run({ correlationId }, async () => {
    56→    logger.info('Starting request'); // ✅ correlation_id present
    57→
    58→    // Async operation that doesn't preserve context
    59→    await someAsyncOperation(); // 🔴 Context lost here!
    60→
    61→    logger.info('Finishing request'); // ❌ correlation_id MISSING
    62→  });
    63→}
    64→```
    65→
    66→❌ **Problem**: Async operations lose the execution context
    67→
    68→## Common Failure Patterns
    69→
    70→### Pattern 1: Forgotten Context Cleanup
    71→
    72→```java
    73→// WRONG - context not cleared
    74→@Component
    75→public class BadFilter extends OncePerRequestFilter {
    76→    @Override
    77→    protected void doFilterInternal(HttpServletRequest request,
    78→                                   HttpServletResponse response,
    79→                                   FilterChain filterChain) throws ServletException, IOException {
    80→        String correlationId = request.getHeader("X-Correlation-ID");
    81→        MDC.put("correlation_id", correlationId);
    82→        filterChain.doFilter(request, response);
    83→        // ❌ Forgot to clear! Next request may see this correlation_id
    84→    }
    85→}
    86→
    87→// CORRECT - always cleanup
    88→@Component
    89→public class GoodFilter extends OncePerRequestFilter {
    90→    @Override
    91→    protected void doFilterInternal(HttpServletRequest request,
    92→                                   HttpServletResponse response,
    93→                                   FilterChain filterChain) throws ServletException, IOException {
    94→        String correlationId = request.getHeader("X-Correlation-ID");
    95→        MDC.put("correlation_id", correlationId);
    96→        try {
    97→            filterChain.doFilter(request, response);
    98→        } finally {
    99→            MDC.remove("correlation_id"); // ✅ Always cleanup
   100→        }
   101→    }
   102→}
   103→```
   104→
   105→### Pattern 2: Async Methods Without Decorator
   106→
   107→```java
   108→// WRONG - correlation_id lost in async thread
   109→@Service
   110→public class BadAsyncService {
   111→    @Async
   112→    public void processOrderAsync(String orderId) {
   113→        // ❌ MDC from original request thread is NOT inherited
   114→        logger.info("Processing order"); // Missing correlation_id!
   115→    }
   116→}
   117→
   118→// CORRECT - configure TaskDecorator
   119→@Configuration
   120→public class AsyncConfiguration implements AsyncConfigurer {
   121→    @Override
   122→    public Executor getAsyncExecutor() {
   123→        ThreadPoolTaskExecutor executor = new ThreadPoolTaskExecutor();
   124→        executor.setTaskDecorator(new ContextPropagatingDecorator());
   125→        executor.initialize();
   126→        return executor;
   127→    }
   128→
   129→    public static class ContextPropagatingDecorator implements TaskDecorator {
   130→        @Override
   131→        public Runnable decorate(Runnable runnable) {
   132→            Map<String, String> contextMap = MDC.getCopyOfContextMap();
   133→            return () -> {
   134→                if (contextMap != null) {
   135→                    MDC.setContextMap(contextMap);
   136→                } else {
   137→                    MDC.clear();
   138→                }
   139→                try {
   140→                    runnable.run();
   141→                } finally {
   142→                    MDC.clear();
   143→                }
   144→            };
   145→        }
   146→    }
   147→
   148→    @Service
   149→    public class GoodAsyncService {
   150→        @Async
   151→        public void processOrderAsync(String orderId) {
   152→            // ✅ Correlation_id properly propagated
   153→            logger.info("Processing order");
   154→        }
   155→    }
   156→}
   157→```
   158→
   159→### Pattern 3: Message Queue Operations
   160→
   161→```java
   162→// WRONG - no correlation context
   163→@KafkaListener(topics = "orders")
   164→public void processOrder(String message) {
   165→    // ❌ Correlation ID from original request is lost
   166→    // Message arrived on different thread with no context
   167→    logger.info("Processing order from queue"); // No correlation_id
   168→}
   169→
   170→// CORRECT - extract and propagate from message
   171→@KafkaListener(topics = "orders")
   172→public void processOrder(String message, @Header("X-Correlation-ID") String correlationId) {
   173→    MDC.put("correlation_id", correlationId);
   174→    try {
   175→        logger.info("Processing order from queue"); // ✅ Has correlation_id
   176→    } finally {
   177→        MDC.clear();
   178→    }
   179→}
   180→```
   181→
   182→### Pattern 4: Retry Logic
   183→
   184→```java
   185→// WRONG - context lost on retry
   186→public String callDownstreamService() {
   187→    try {
   188→        return restTemplate.getForObject(url, String.class);
   189→    } catch (Exception e) {
   190→        // ❌ Retry happens on different thread, loses MDC
   191→        return retry();
   192→    }
   193→}
   194→
   195→// CORRECT - use resilience4j with context propagation
   196→@Service
   197→public class ResilientService {
   198→    private final Resilience4jCircuitBreakerFactory factory;
   199→
   200→    public String callDownstreamService() {
   201→        Retry retry = factory.create("order-service-retry",
   202→            RetryConfig.custom()
   203→                .retryExceptions(IOException.class)
   204→                .build());
   205→
   206→        // ✅ resilience4j can be configured to preserve MDC
   207→        return Decorators.retry(retry)
   208→            .decorate(() -> restTemplate.getForObject(url, String.class))
   209→            .execute();
   210→    }
   211→}
   212→```
   213→
   214→## Technology-Specific Solutions
   215→
   216→### Java/Spring Boot: TransmittableThreadLocal (TTL)
   217→
   218→**Problem**: InheritableThreadLocal doesn't work with thread pools
   219→
   220→**Solution**: Use `TransmittableThreadLocal` library
   221→
   222→```xml
   223→<dependency>
   224→    <groupId>com.alibaba</groupId>
   225→    <artifactId>transmittable-thread-local</artifactId>
   226→    <version>2.14.2</version>
   227→</dependency>
   228→```
   229→
   230→```java
   231→// Setup TTL for MDC
   232→TransmittableThreadLocal<Map<String, String>> mdcTtl = new TransmittableThreadLocal<>();
   233→
   234→// Configure thread pool to use TTL
   235→@Bean
   236→public Executor taskExecutor() {
   237→    ThreadPoolTaskExecutor executor = new ThreadPoolTaskExecutor();
   238→    executor.setTaskDecorator(new TtlTaskDecorator());
   239→    executor.initialize();
   240→    return executor;
   241→}
   242→
   243→public class TtlTaskDecorator implements TaskDecorator {
   244→    @Override
   245→    public Runnable decorate(Runnable runnable) {
   246→        // TTL automatically handles context propagation
   247→        return TtlRunnable.get(runnable);
   248→    }
   249→}
   250→```
   251→
   252→### Python: contextvars (Built-in)
   253→
   254→**Solution**: Python 3.7+ includes `contextvars` for async-safe context
   255→
   256→```python
   257→import contextvars
   258→import asyncio
   259→
   260→# Define context variable
   261→correlation_id_var = contextvars.ContextVar('correlation_id')
   262→
   263→# In middleware
   264→async def bind_correlation_id(request, call_next):
   265→    correlation_id = request.headers.get('X-Correlation-ID')
   266→    token = correlation_id_var.set(correlation_id) # ✅ Set for this context
   267→    try:
   268→        response = await call_next(request)
   269→    finally:
   270→        correlation_id_var.reset(token) # ✅ Clean up
   271→
   272→# In any async function
   273→async def process_order(order_id: str):
   274→    corr_id = correlation_id_var.get() # ✅ Works in any async context
   275→    logger.info("Processing", correlation_id=corr_id)
   276→
   277→    # Even nested async calls work
   278→    await asyncio.gather(
   279→        validate_order(order_id),
   280→        check_inventory(order_id)
   281→    ) # ✅ Both preserve correlation_id
   282→```
   283→
   284→### Node.js: AsyncLocalStorage or AsyncContext
   285→
   286→**Solution**: Use `AsyncLocalStorage` for async context
   287→
   288→```javascript
   289→const { AsyncLocalStorage } = require('async_hooks');
   290→
   291→const correlationIdStore = new AsyncLocalStorage();
   292→
   293→// Middleware
   294→app.use((req, res, next) => {
   295→  const correlationId = req.headers['x-correlation-id'];
   296→  correlationIdStore.run({ correlationId }, () => {
   297→    next();
   298→  });
   299→});
   300→
   301→// Get logger with correlation_id
   302→function getLogger() {
   303→  const context = correlationIdStore.getStore();
   304→  return logger.child({ correlation_id: context?.correlationId });
   305→}
   306→
   307→// Usage - works with promises and async/await
   308→app.get('/orders/:id', async (req, res) => {
   309→  getLogger().info('Fetching order'); // ✅ correlation_id present
   310→
   311→  const inventory = await fetch('http://inventory-service/check');
   312→
   313→  getLogger().info('Inventory checked'); // ✅ Still present
   314→  res.json({});
   315→});
   316→
   317→// Background tasks - must explicitly propagate
   318→async function processOrderAsync(correlationId) {
   319→  await correlationIdStore.run({ correlationId }, async () => {
   320→    getLogger().info('Processing background order'); // ✅ Has correlation_id
   321→    await someAsyncWork();
   322→  });
   323→}
   324→```
   325→
   326→## Testing Correlation ID Propagation
   327→
   328→### Unit Test: Verify Context Cleanup
   329→
   330→```java
   331→@Test
   332→void testMDCIsCleanedAfterRequest() {
   333→    // Before
   334→    assertNull(MDC.get("correlation_id"));
   335→
   336→    // Simulate request with correlation_id
   337→    String testId = "test-123";
   338→    MDC.put("correlation_id", testId);
   339→    assertEquals(testId, MDC.get("correlation_id"));
   340→
   341→    // After cleanup (as filter should do)
   342→    MDC.clear();
   343→
   344→    // Verify cleaned
   345→    assertNull(MDC.get("correlation_id"));
   346→}
   347→```
   348→
   349→### Integration Test: Async Propagation
   350→
   351→```java
   352→@Test
   353→void testCorrelationIdPropagatedToAsyncTask() throws Exception {
   354→    String correlationId = "async-test-123";
   355→    MDC.put("correlation_id", correlationId);
   356→
   357→    AtomicReference<String> asyncMdcValue = new AtomicReference<>();
   358→
   359→    asyncService.processAsync(() -> {
   360→        asyncMdcValue.set(MDC.get("correlation_id"));
   361→    });
   362→
   363→    // Wait for async completion
   364→    Thread.sleep(100);
   365→
   366→    assertEquals(correlationId, asyncMdcValue.get());
   367→    MDC.clear();
   368→}
   369→```
   370→
   371→### End-to-End Test: Service Boundary
   372→
   373→```javascript
   374→describe('Correlation ID Propagation', () => {
   375→  it('should propagate correlation_id across service calls', async () => {
   376→    const correlationId = 'e2e-test-123';
   377→
   378→    const response1 = await request(app)
   379→      .get('/orders')
   380→      .set('X-Correlation-ID', correlationId);
   381→
   382→    // Extract correlation_id from log output
   383→    const logs = captureConsoleOutput();
   384→    expect(logs).toContain(correlationId);
   385→
   386→    // Call downstream service
   387→    const response2 = await request(downstreamService)
   388→      .get('/inventory')
   389→      .set('X-Correlation-ID', correlationId);
   390→
   391→    const downstreamLogs = captureConsoleOutput(downstreamService);
   392→    expect(downstreamLogs).toContain(correlationId);
   393→  });
   394→
   395→  it('should generate new correlation_id if header missing', async () => {
   396→    const response = await request(app).get('/orders');
   397→
   398→    const logs = captureConsoleOutput();
   399→    // Should have some correlation_id (UUID format)
   400→    expect(logs).toMatch(/correlation_id":"[a-f0-9\-]{36}/);
   401→  });
   402→});
   403→```
   404→
   405→## Checklist for Async Safety
   406→
   407→- [ ] All ThreadLocal usage has try-finally cleanup
   408→- [ ] TaskDecorator configured for thread pools (@Async, custom executors)
   409→- [ ] contextvars/AsyncLocalStorage used for async code (not ThreadLocal)
   410→- [ ] Message queue handlers extract correlation_id from headers
   411→- [ ] Retry logic preserves MDC/context
   412→- [ ] Background jobs receive correlation_id explicitly
   413→- [ ] Integration tests verify async propagation
   414→- [ ] No correlation_id bleeding between unrelated requests
   415→- [ ] Context cleared after each request
   416→
