### 2.8 [IMPROVED] Log Aggregation Prerequisites and Validation

**CRITICAL**: Before implementing logging, validate log aggregation platform is healthy, accessible, and ready.

**Pre-Deployment Validation Checklist**:

```bash
# 1. Verify ELK/Splunk/Datadog/CloudWatch is accessible
curl -u ${ES_USER}:${ES_PASSWORD} https://elasticsearch:9200/_cluster/health
# Expected: HTTP 200, "status": "green"

# 2. Test write permissions
curl -X POST https://elasticsearch:9200/test-index/_doc \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"test": "write", "timestamp": "2025-04-03T00:00:00Z"}'
# Expected: HTTP 201, "_id" in response

# 3. Test read permissions
curl -u ${ES_USER}:${ES_PASSWORD} https://elasticsearch:9200/test-index/_search
# Expected: HTTP 200, hits array returns

# 4. Verify retention policies configured
curl https://elasticsearch:9200/_ilm/policy | jq '.[] | {name, phases}'
# Expected: policies with delete phase configured

# 5. Verify storage capacity
curl https://elasticsearch:9200/_cat/nodes?h=name,disk.percent
# Expected: disk usage <80%

# 6. Verify network connectivity from each service
for service in order-service payment-service inventory-service; do
  nc -zv elasticsearch:9200
done
# Expected: All services can reach elasticsearch

# 7. Load aggregation platform credentials into secret management
# Store in environment or secret manager:
# - ES_USER / ES_PASSWORD
# - DATADOG_API_KEY
# - AWS credentials for CloudWatch
# - etc.
```

**Infrastructure Readiness Validation Script** (`scripts/validate-aggregation.js`):

```javascript
const elasticsearch = require('@elastic/elasticsearch');

async function validateAggregationPlatform() {
  const client = new elasticsearch.Client({
    node: process.env.ELASTICSEARCH_URL,
    auth: {
      username: process.env.ES_USER,
      password: process.env.ES_PASSWORD
    }
  });

  const checks = {
    connectivity: false,
    writeable: false,
    readable: false,
    storage: false,
    retention: false
  };

  try {
    // Check connectivity
    const health = await client.cluster.health();
    checks.connectivity = health.status === 'green';
    console.log(`✓ Connectivity: ${checks.connectivity}`);

    // Check write permissions
    const writeTest = await client.index({
      index: 'test-logs',
      body: { test: true, timestamp: new Date().toISOString() }
    });
    checks.writeable = writeTest.result === 'created';
    console.log(`✓ Write permissions: ${checks.writeable}`);

    // Check read permissions
    const searchTest = await client.search({ index: 'test-logs' });
    checks.readable = searchTest.hits.total >= 0;
    console.log(`✓ Read permissions: ${checks.readable}`);

    // Check storage
    const nodes = await client.cat.nodes({ format: 'json' });
    const diskPercent = nodes[0].disk_percent || 0;
    checks.storage = diskPercent < 80;
    console.log(`✓ Storage capacity: ${diskPercent}% used (threshold 80%)`);

    // Check retention policy
    const policy = await client.ilm.getLifecycle({ policy: 'default-policy' });
    checks.retention = !!policy.policies;
    console.log(`✓ Retention policy: ${checks.retention}`);

    // Summary
    const allPassed = Object.values(checks).every(v => v);
    if (allPassed) {
      console.log('\n✓ All validation checks passed. Ready for deployment.');
      process.exit(0);
    } else {
      console.error('\n✗ Some validation checks failed. See above.');
      process.exit(1);
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Validation failed:', error.message);
    process.exit(1);
  }
}

validateAggregationPlatform();
```

