### Cost Analysis and Log Volume Projections

**Log Volume Calculator**:

```bash
# Estimate log volume based on request rate

Average request rate: 1000 req/sec
Logs per request: 3 (request start, processing, response)
Log size: 500 bytes per log (JSON with context)

Daily volume = 1000 req/sec × 86400 sec × 3 logs × 500 bytes
            = 129.6 GB per day
            = 3.9 TB per month

Storage with retention policy:
30-day retention: 3.9 TB × 30 = 117 TB
90-day retention: 3.9 TB × 90 = 351 TB

Cost estimates (AWS CloudWatch):
$0.50 per GB ingested + $0.03 per GB stored
Daily cost: 129.6 GB × $0.50 = $64.80
Monthly cost: ~$1,944 + storage costs

# Use this calculator for your environment
npm run calculate:log-volume -- --req-per-sec 1000 --retention-days 30
```

**Cost Optimization Strategies**:

| Strategy | Implementation | Potential Savings |
|----------|-----------------|-------------------|
| **Sampling** | Send 1 in N logs to aggregator | 70-90% |
| **Log Level Configuration** | INFO in prod, DEBUG in dev | 30-50% |
| **Retention Policy** | Delete logs >30 days | 20-40% |
| **Compression** | Compress archived logs | 50-70% |
| **Selective Indexing** | Index only critical fields | 20-30% |

**Recommended Configuration**:
- Production: INFO level, 30-day retention
- Staging: DEBUG level, 7-day retention
- Development: TRACE level, 1-day retention

