**Feature Flag Rollout Plan:**

| Stage | Timeline | Coverage | Action |
|-------|----------|----------|--------|
| **Stage 1** | Day 1-2 | 10% of requests | Enable on test endpoints only |
| **Stage 2** | Day 3 | 50% of requests | If no issues, expand to 50% |
| **Stage 3** | Day 4-5 | 100% of requests | Full enablement or disable in <30s |

**Feature Flag Granularity:**
- Minimum: Per-service enable/disable (e.g., `correlation-id-logging:user-service`)
- Recommended: Per-endpoint enable/disable (e.g., `correlation-id-logging:user-service:/users/*`)
- **Requirement**: Disable must not require code redeployment (configuration change only)

**Rollout Safety:**
- Enable feature flag immediately in all deployed code
- Keep correlation ID middleware active (always capture)
- Feature flag only controls whether logs include correlation context
- Disable decision: If p99 latency >5ms or error rate increases, disable in <30s without redeployment

